# Public-site SEO

- SEO applies to apps/site only. Cockpit, field, and client portal are authenticated, noindex, and absent from the sitemap.
- robots.txt controls crawl. noindex controls indexing. Do not disallow a URL whose noindex must be read.
- A sitemap is a hint, not proof of indexing. Include only canonical, indexable, public, useful URLs.
- Do not promise rankings, invent keyword volume, or invent Search Console data.
- Structured data must match visible content. Do not invent ratings, reviews, prices, authors, or dates.
- llms.txt is not a Google ranking strategy.
- No indexable public page until the legal name and canonical host exist.
